### Limitations the authors admit
- 2018PASJ...70...73H: SFR may be underestimated by about a factor of 2; central region feedback uncertain
- 2018ApJ...855L..25K: Dust temperature assumption is the largest uncertainty (up to factor ~2); MIREX has zero-point offsets, saturation and MIR-source contamination.
- 2014ApJ...786..114L: Disk is not well resolved, so its radius is an upper limit and the temperature index is rough; model is simple and symmetric and excludes outflow, jet and extended envelope.
- 2019MNRAS.486.2366M: Temperature, velocity gradient and density poorly constrained and correlated
- 2020ApJ...894...87C: Large systematic uncertainties in virial parameters (temperature, mass, distance), so supervirial vs subvirial unclear
- 2020ApJ...894...87C: Many cores are not well resolved
- 2025SciA...11.4512O: Mass of ALMA1 is an upper limit under optically thin approximation; infall is neither free-fall nor viscous
- 2025SciA...11.4512O: Red-shifted streamer excluded from methanol analysis due to outflow contamination
- 2020A&A...643A..89P: Inner outflow fluxes uncertain due to broad nuclear profile; CO(4–3) excess unexplained
- 2024ApJ...966...51G: LTE assumptions, possibly optically thin 12CO; sensitivity limited to several Msun/pc^2
- 2024ApJ...966...51G: 8um may trace gas column rather than star formation at these scales
- 2024ApJ...972..111L: Only projected distances and radial velocities known; spatial offset of redshifted [C II] smaller than beam
- 2015Natur.525..218R: NW ALMA flux is lower than APEX; may reflect different line ratio, weak emission or resolved-out extended emission
- 2018ApJ...863..193V: The cavity is poorly defined and may not be real
- 2018ApJ...863..193V: HST images manually aligned, so small-scale offsets between gas and UV may be missed
- 2014ApJ...785..149S: Single-component modelling of a heterogeneous sample; no single model fits (chi2 min 10.4 for 3 dof); degeneracies remain; differential magnification not accounted
- 2019ApJ...881L...2B: 868 GHz measured four days from the others, longer than variability coherence time
- 2020MNRAS.493.4294B: Uncertainty in C not included in M_dyn; CMB attenuation of [C II] not corrected; resolution does not resolve outflow regions
- 2017A&A...601A..48G: Cosmic-ray ionization rate poorly constrained; full sensitivity study left for future
- 2014ApJ...795L..25R: Core unresolved so density is a lower limit; deviation may be from temperature
- 2024ApJ...963....1O: X_CO uncertainty may overestimate molecular mass by a factor of a few
- 2024ApJ...963....1O: Chandra data too shallow to resolve cavity
- 2015ApJ...811...92C: Model is parametric, not dynamically consistent, no systematic parameter search
- 2015ApJ...811...92C: MEM resolution varies with image
- 2017ApJ...842L..24A: Peak brightness cannot be converted to density without non-LTE excitation modelling, which needs more than one line.
- 2017ApJ...842L..24A: Models are non-rotating and omit chemistry, so SASI signatures cannot be assessed.
- 2014Sci...345.1584B: Preliminary LTE model not fully optimized for ALMA; abundance uncertainties exclude free-free contamination and dust property uncertainties
- 2020ApJ...891...64F: Lens model poorly constrained; magnification uncertain by a factor of a few
- 2025ApJ...986..195L: J0834 fit is unreliable due to an anomalous UV bump and a dominant AGN
- 2018ApJ...857...19F: Missed flux relative to APEX (median 63% recovered), possibly low surface brightness emission
- 2018ApJ...857...19F: Sampled range of environments limited to inner rising rotation curve
- 2017ApJ...834..178Y: Only three protostars with M*<0.1 Msun; larger low-mass sample required
- 2017ApJ...834..178Y: Masses and disk radii of IRAS 15398 and IRAS 16253 are lower and upper limits
- 2015ApJ...812...27A: Inclination poorly constrained by the disk model; mass estimates are uncertain by optical depth, temperature, abundance
- 2015ApJ...812...27A: PV mean-position method underestimates break radius at limited resolution
- 2017MNRAS.465.4390B: Low resolution; size measurement uncertain, close to beam size
- 2017MNRAS.465.4390B: Results depend on assumed dust SED
- 2020MNRAS.499.2534K: Mid-IR resolution blends sources; ages and masses uncertain
- 2025A&A...699A.369V: Most clumps unresolved; missing extended flux without Total Power data; non-LTE modeling out of scope
- 2020ApJ...892..147S: Only one cloud, so not statistically significant
- 2024ApJ...964..166K: Comparison depends on assumed X_CO and R21 and on resolution differences; starburst differences are ambiguous
- 2024ApJ...961..120C: Radio resolution cannot identify which of B, C, G hosts the AGN; spectral index from only two points plus limits
- 2024ApJ...961..120C: 5 arcsec ATCA-ASKAP offset unexplained
- 2012ApJ...760L..25E: Clumps mostly unresolved; higher resolution needed; short spacings needed
- 2012ApJ...760L..25E: Inclination of the arm is uncertain
- 2017ApJ...836..130R: XCO uncertainty raises mass uncertainty to a factor of a few
- 2013MNRAS.432....2K: Counts below the LESS flux limit are biased because fields were targeted near brighter sources
- 2017ApJ...849...91M: High-z sample biased to high luminosities
- 2019ApJ...872..121U: Abundance uncertainty up to a factor of 2 affects masses
- 2020A&A...642A.155Z: Single lines cannot give definitive redshifts
- 2019A&A...628A..27B: Ages unreliable because the same accretion history is assumed for all sources; no CR attenuation.
- 2015MNRAS.449..715W: Mass estimates uncertain due to cloud boundary definition and a factor ~2 systematics; gas temperature measured only for G0.253
- 2017PASJ...69...18T: Abundance and Tex adopted from Galactic/other measurements; may vary cloud to cloud
- 2019ApJ...875...24C: Single temperature and filling factor assumptions fail in hubs
- 2014ApJ...796..131O: Missing flux on large scales biases rotation velocities at large radii
- 2014ApJ...796..131O: SO is optically thick so density and abundance unconstrained
- 2018MNRAS.477.4380S: Dust parameters cannot be simultaneously constrained; clump conditions assumed equal to galaxy-wide
- 2018MNRAS.477.4380S: Magnetic fields unavailable and neglected
- 2023MNRAS.526.4402B: Mass uncertain by factor of few from dust emissivity; interferometric missing flux and gas-to-dust ratio may bias masses
- 2025NatAs...9.1833L: Masses are lower limits due to optical depth and missing flux
- 2025NatAs...9.1833L: Secondary disks cannot be confirmed with current sensitivity and resolution
- 2025A&A...700A.165B: Current data cannot distinguish between scenarios
- 2024A&A...690A..55S: Halo mass estimates carry large uncertainties; group centre and concentration degeneracies; interloper contamination
- 2024A&A...690A..55S: Cold-stream regime scatter based on only six points
- 2012A&A...538L...9H: Missing short spacings lose about half of single-dish flux; errors exclude this
- 2016MNRAS.458.3134R: Systemic velocity from emission lines may be offset from the stellar potential; line-of-sight location unconstrained
- 2016MNRAS.458.3134R: X_CO uncertain by a factor of a few
- 2015ApJ...806L..17S: The pressure estimate has considerable uncertainty
- 2018Sci...362.1034D: U1 may be at a different redshift; stellar mass and SFR uncertain by factor of 2
- 2018ApJ...868...95M: Four lines constrain many parameters giving broad probability functions; single-phase assumption inappropriate
- 2018ApJ...868...95M: Sensitivity insufficient for meaningful upper limit at North-OF-Blue
- 2019ApJ...884...48C: Dust temperature poorly constrained; higher core temperatures would lower masses and raise alpha_total
- 2019ApJ...884...48C: Velocity dispersion extrapolated via an assumed Kolmogorov law
- 2013A&A...560A.103M: Cannot distinguish infall+Keplerian from pure Keplerian in outer 30 AU due to low S/N; foreground absorption
- 2017ApJ...844..123F: Redshifts of non-QSO SMGs unknown (assumed 2.5), making their results less reliable
- 2017ApJ...844..123F: Size measurements at SNR<10 are biased high
- 2017ApJ...844..123F: Duty cycle is an upper limit since no BH accretion assumed in SMGs without QSOs
- 2020ApJ...890...76N: Simple infall models fail to reproduce the deep HCO+ absorption
- 2025ApJ...995..193Y: Conclusive classification requires chemical evolution analysis; N2D+ only marginally detected.
- 2020ApJ...903...94M: Magnetic field properties in the molecular phase unknown
- 2025A&A...696A..31G: Gas temperatures poorly constrained by HCNH+; large-scale emission filtered; beam dilution neglected
- 2025ApJ...995..219F: Lens model systematics not included; mass-sheet degeneracy possibly unbroken
- 2025ApJ...995..219F: Gas mass is a lower limit given alpha_CO
- 2014ApJ...795..156W: Small sample, selection effects, superposition and low-number statistics
- 2016ApJ...832..148V: Only 43% of single-dish flux recovered; missing short spacings
- 2014A&A...568A..92M: Knot C in rest-frame optical poorly fitted by the lens model
- 2018ApJ...866..117C: AGN continuum non-detection may reflect lack of sensitivity
- 2016ApJ...823..160D: Mass uncertainties dominated by dust temperature and opacity assumptions
- 2016ApJ...823..160D: Only two simulations; full parameter space needed
- 2014ApJ...791..123W: Explosive-center identification needs more theory and observation
- 2018Natur.556..469M: Dynamical mass is an upper limit if not virialized; line-of-sight projection cannot be completely ruled out
- 2020ApJ...896..110L: Cannot discriminate causes of broad line widths in cores with the data at hand; filament pressure not computed
- 2025A&A...695A.236L: Momentum and energy not corrected for unknown inclination
- 2020MNRAS.496..364R: Tex assumes optically thin LTE, which the results contradict; covering factors give lower limits on tau
- 2024PASA...41...76Z: Only line-of-sight velocity and CO traced mass are measured, so acceleration and central mass are underestimated
- 2025MNRAS.536.3757A: Modest resolution may misclassify mergers as disks
- 2018ApJ...869..126L: Gas mass uncertain by ~0.4-0.5 dex from Tdust, kappa and DGR; sources may break up at higher resolution
- 2018ApJ...869..126L: Cannot distinguish free-free contamination at 350 GHz from synchrotron at 36 GHz with two bands
- 2019ApJ...871..100H: Offset smaller than beam; calibration issue or proper motion not excluded
- 2015ApJ...804...37L: Kinematic analysis preliminary since arm inclinations unknown
- 2018ApJ...856...72O: SFRs assume ALESS template for all components; mass estimates highly uncertain
- 2020MNRAS.496..394R: Single excitation temperature is a large source of uncertainty.
- 2020MNRAS.496..394R: Spectral index poorly constrained because bands 6 and 7 are adjacent; fluxes and globule mass are lower bounds.
- 2024A&A...690A.375S: sigma_nt along line of sight only; 3D dispersion likely higher
- 2020MNRAS.495.3840M: alpha_CO may be a factor of a few lower in the bar, so Sigma_mol could be overestimated
- 2020MNRAS.495.3840M: SFR below 1e-3 Msun/yr/kpc2 should be considered upper limits
- 2019ApJ...881...10B: Model not a formally acceptable fit (chi^2_nu=1.179); correlated noise; local irregularities in velocity/dispersion fields
- 2019ApJ...881...10B: Distance disagreements among estimates imply M_BH may lie in (2.0-3.8)e9 Msun
- 2018MNRAS.477.2760M: Model comparison is only qualitative; DCF validity uncertain; interferometric filtering of large scales
- 2014ApJ...793...37A: Marginally resolved clumps have large radius uncertainties; only 4 of 13 clumps deconvolved.
- 2019PASJ...71...71H: M_dyn uncertain by at least a factor of three; virial theorem may not apply.
- 2019PASJ...71...71H: Clump continuum fluxes may be contaminated by each other at current resolution.
- 2020ApJ...890..129K: Mass uncertainty from dust opacity exceeds one order of magnitude
- 2024A&A...690A.376S: Model applicability limited: fibers are non-isothermal prolate spheroids; pressure estimates assume equilibrium
- 2019ApJ...871..170M: Rgd for diffuse Milky Way gas may not apply to the dense CMZ
- 2019ApJ...871..170M: H3O+/SO ratio affected by optical depth and calibration; factor of two differences possible
- 2019ApJ...871..170M: Total Power data unusable so no zero-spacing beyond ACA
- 2018A&A...618L...5N: Higher sensitivity and resolution are needed to confirm the lack of outflow
- 2012A&A...544L...7P: Model has more parameters than can be constrained due to degeneracies
- 2017MNRAS.469.4683C: Clump SFRs vary by up to ~1 dex between methods and clump R51/alpha_CO are poorly constrained

